msgid "The program arguments have an unclosed quote."
msgstr ""

msgid "The debugger is not available yet. It will use Delve in a future version."
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Delve (dlv) was not found: {executable}\n"
"Install it with:\n"
"    {command}\n"
"or set its path in Tools > Options > Environment."
msgstr ""

msgid "Delve stopped unexpectedly."
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Variable \"{name}\" is never used"
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"You created the variable \"{name}\" but never read it. Go refuses to "
"compile code with unused variables, because they are usually a mistake or"
" leftover code."
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Use \"{name}\" somewhere (for example, print it), delete it, or replace "
"it with _ if you must receive a value you do not need."
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Package \"{package}\" is imported but never used"
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The file imports the package \"{package}\", but no code uses it. Go does "
"not allow unused imports, to keep programs clean and fast to compile."
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Delete the line that imports \"{package}\", or use something from it."
msgstr ""

msgid "The function can end without returning a value"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This function says it returns a value, but there is a way to reach its "
"closing brace without a return statement. For example, an if returns a "
"value but the case where the condition is false does not."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Add a return statement at the end of the function, or an else branch that"
" also returns a value."
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid "\"{name}\" is private to package {package}"
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"In Go, only names that start with a capital letter can be used from "
"another package. \"{name}\" starts with a lowercase letter, so package "
"{package} keeps it private, or the real name has different capital "
"letters."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Write the name exactly as the package documents it, starting with a "
"capital letter (for example strings.ToUpper, not strings.toUpper)."
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Unknown name: {name}"
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Go does not know anything called \"{name}\". It was never declared, it is"
" declared in a place this code cannot see (such as inside another "
"function or block), or it is misspelled."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Check the spelling and the capital letters, declare the variable before "
"you use it (for example with :=), or import the package it belongs to."
msgstr ""

msgid "The variable already exists: use = instead of :="
msgstr ""

msgid ""
":= creates new variables. Every variable on its left side already exists "
"in this block, so there is nothing new to create."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Use = to change the value of an existing variable. Use := only the first "
"time."
msgstr ""

msgid "The program has no main function"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A Go program starts running in the function main of package main. This "
"package is called main, but it does not contain a function named main."
msgstr ""

msgid "Add a function with exactly this header: func main() {{ ... }}"
msgstr ""

msgid "This file is not a runnable program"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Only code in package main can be run. The first line of this file "
"declares a different package, which Go treats as a library."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Change the first line to: package main (and make sure there is a func "
"main)."
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Package \"{package}\" was not found"
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Go cannot find the package \"{package}\". Standard packages have fixed "
"names (fmt, math, strings, os...), and packages from the internet must be"
" added to your module before you can import them."
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Check the spelling of the import path. For an external package, run go "
"get {package} in a folder that has a go.mod file."
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Index {index} is out of range"
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The program tried to use position {index}, but the slice, array or string"
" only has {length} element(s). Valid positions go from 0 to {length} - 1."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Check the index before using it (for example: if i < len(items)) and "
"remember that counting starts at 0."
msgstr ""

msgid "Writing to a map that was never created"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The map variable was declared but never created, so it is nil. You can "
"read from a nil map, but writing to it stops the program."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Create the map before writing to it: ages := make(map[string]int) or ages"
" := map[string]int{{}}."
msgstr ""

msgid "Using a pointer that is nil"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The program read or wrote through a pointer (or an interface, map or "
"slice element holding one) whose value is nil, so it points to nothing."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Make sure the pointer gets a value before you use it, for example p := "
"&Person{{}} or p := new(Person), or check if p != nil first."
msgstr ""

msgid "Deadlock: every goroutine is waiting forever"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"All goroutines are blocked waiting for each other, so nothing can "
"continue. Usually a channel is sent to with nobody receiving, or received"
" from with nobody sending, or a WaitGroup or Mutex is never released."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Make sure another goroutine receives what you send (go func() {{ ... "
"}}()), use a buffered channel, close the channel when you are done, or "
"call wg.Done()."
msgstr ""

msgid "Division by zero"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The program divided an integer by zero (with / or %). That has no result,"
" so Go stops the program."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Check that the divisor is not 0 before dividing, for example: if people "
"!= 0 {{ ... }}."
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Slice limits [{bounds}] are out of range"
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The program tried to take the part [{bounds}] of a slice or string, but "
"those limits go past its end, or the start is bigger than the end."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Make sure that 0 <= start <= end <= len(s) before slicing, for example "
"with min(end, len(s))."
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Type assertion failed: {actual} is not {type}"
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The program asserted that a value holds a {type}, but it actually holds a"
" {actual}. A failed assertion with a single result stops the program."
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Use the two-result form to check safely: n, ok := value.({type}). Or use "
"a type switch."
msgstr ""

msgid "A curly brace {{ }} is missing"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Every {{ needs a matching }}. Go reached the end of the file, or of a "
"block, while it was still waiting for one. Go also needs the opening {{ "
"on the same line as func, if, for or else."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Count your {{ and }} and add the missing one. Keep each opening {{ at the"
" end of the line that starts the block."
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Syntax error: unexpected {token}"
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Go could not understand this line. It found {token} in a place where Go's"
" grammar does not allow it. The real mistake is often just before that "
"point."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Look right before the marked position for a missing comma, parenthesis, "
"quote or operator."
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Wrong type: a {type} was expected"
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The value {value} does not have the type {type}, which is what Go expects"
" here. Go never converts between types such as int and string "
"automatically."
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Use a value of type {type}, or convert it explicitly, for example with "
"int(x), float64(x) or strconv.Itoa(n)."
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Cannot combine {left_type} and {right_type}"
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"In {expression} the two sides have different types ({left_type} and "
"{right_type}). Operators such as +, - or == only work between values of "
"the same type."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Convert one side so both have the same type, for example strconv.Itoa(n) "
"to turn an int into a string, or float64(n) to mix it with decimals."
msgstr ""

msgid "The number of variables and values does not match"
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The left side of = or := has {left} variable(s), but the right side gives"
" {right} value(s). Both numbers must be equal. Many functions, such as "
"strconv.Atoi, return two values: a result and an error."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Add or remove variables until both sides match, for example: number, err "
":= strconv.Atoi(text). Use _ for a value you do not need."
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Not enough arguments for {function}"
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The function {function} needs more values than you passed. In the "
"original message, \"have\" lists what you passed and \"want\" lists what "
"it expects."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Pass one value for each parameter, in the same order and with the right "
"types."
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Too many arguments for {function}"
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The function {function} receives fewer values than you passed. In the "
"original message, \"have\" lists what you passed and \"want\" lists what "
"it expects."
msgstr ""

msgid "Remove the extra values so there is exactly one for each parameter."
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid "The format of {function} does not match its values"
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format, python-format
msgid ""
"The format text given to {function} does not match the values after it. "
"Each verb such as %d, %s or %v needs exactly one value, of a suitable "
"type."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Add or remove values so there is one per verb, or use fmt.Println if you "
"do not need formatting."
msgstr ""

msgid "This code can never run"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"These statements come after a return, panic, break or infinite loop, so "
"the program can never reach them."
msgstr ""

msgid "Delete the unreachable lines, or move them before the return."
msgstr ""

